# Build context: what must NEVER enter the image.
#
# `node_modules` first, and this isn't an optimization: the Dockerfile runs
# `pnpm install` THEN `COPY . .`. Without this exclusion, the host machine's
# node_modules (Windows/macOS native binaries) overwrites the Linux
# dependencies just installed, and the build breaks — or worse, silently
# produces a broken image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs: rebuilt inside the image, never copied in.
dist
out-tsc
.angular
coverage

# Local history and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Field notes, gitignored and out of place in an image
*.local.md

# Python tooling environments (have no business being here)
.venv
.venv-*

# Docs and dev files that don't change the served binary
docs
*.md
!README.md
